  "facts": [
    "The Karmøy Tunnel, 8.9 kilometres long, held Norway's title as the longest subsea road tunnel from its 2013 opening until Ryfast opened in 2019.",
    "Opened in September 2013 as part of the T-Link toll project, the tunnel features an underground roundabout at Fosen that links to a shorter tunnel heading north toward Haugesund.",
    "Beneath the Karmsundet strait, Førresfjorden, and even the northern edge of Norsk Hydro's Karmøy facility, the Karmøy Tunnel burrows 8.9 kilometres beneath the sea."
  ],
